  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Civic Space Advancement Project CSAP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Specific objectives: 1: To strengthen the capacity and resilience of civil society actors to protect, promote and monitor human rights in Rwanda. 2: To empower CBOs and citizens to monitor and claim access to socio-economic and environmental rights across community-driven initiatives. 3: To enhance medical service liability by promoting patients&#x2019; rights awareness and ensuring accountability of health-care service providers.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To enhance civic space for civil society in promoting human rights and strengthening democracy in Rwanda To enhance civic space for civil society in promoting human rights and strengthening democracy in Rwanda The Civic Space Advancement Project (CSAP) is a collaborative initiative in Rwanda, focusing on the sector of Government and civil society. Democratic participation and civil society. Funded by Norwegian People&apos;s Aid, the project aims to enhance civic space for civil society in promoting human rights and strengthening democracy in Rwanda. The project encompasses several components, including capacity building for civil society actors, legal aid for human rights defenders, and advocacy for policy changes that foster a favorable environment for patient-centric healthcare services. The project&apos;s scope is outlined in the attached Project Document, which includes a detailed budget. The partnership aims to reduce imbalances between parties and create a more equitable donor-recipient relationship.</narrative>
  </description>
